# Story: three windows arranged, and one of them goes into the Dock. The browser that shared a column with it fills the column now: to the
# eye there is no column of two. The key that moves a window to the right moves it past its neighbour at the first press, and that is
# all that happens: they trade places, at the sizes they had. (It used to take the browser out of a group nobody could see: the same
# picture, both windows narrower, and "moved" for an answer. To a person: it would not dock on the right.)
# A key acts on what a person sees: one press, one step that shows.
# Reference: IDEAS I21.
quiet
open Safari 900x700
open Terminal 700x500
open Chrome 1000x700
arrange
expect above 101 102
expect left-of 101 103

minimize 102
focus 101
expect left-of 101 103
expect size 101 557x851
expect size 103 557x851

# To the left there is nothing, whatever the tree holds: it says so, on screen, and moves nothing.
press dock left
expect fail
expect said already at the left edge
expect left-of 101 103
expect size 101 557x851

# One press.
press dock right
expect ok
expect left-of 103 101
expect size 101 557x851
expect size 103 557x851
expect focused 101

# Out of the Dock again, Terminal is back below the window it shared a column with, and nobody is squeezed for it.
restore 102
expect above 101 102
expect left-of 103 101
expect left-of 103 102
expect size 103 557x851

# A column that shows is a column: there the first press takes the window out of it, as ever.
focus 101
press dock left
expect ok
expect left-of 103 101
expect left-of 101 102
